# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-wildcat/blob/main/src/HooksFactory.sol#L491
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-wildcat/blob/main/src/HooksFactory.sol#L393
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-wildcat/blob/main/src/HooksFactory.sol#L201


# Vulnerability details


## Impact
The deployMarket function does not check if the template for the specified hooksInstance is actually enabled. As a result any user can deploy a market on an existing hooks instance that had its template disabled.
If the user needs a clean hooks instance, he can predeploy several instances of that hook and use those after the template is disabled. Also hooks that dont keep borrower/market specific state, and anyone can deploy a market on, will effectively be forever enabled as users won't need to deploy a new instance to use it. This also has the potential to create future problems if the template is found to have bugs/vulnerabilities.

## Proof of Concept
The vulnerable function is deployMarket() in HooksFactory. It fetches the hooks template details without checking if it is enabled:

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-wildcat/blob/main/src/HooksFactory.sol#L491
```js
  function deployMarket(
    DeployMarketInputs calldata parameters,
    bytes calldata hooksData,
    bytes32 salt,
    address originationFeeAsset,
    uint256 originationFeeAmount
  ) external override nonReentrant returns (address market) {
    if (!IWildcatArchController(_archController).isRegisteredBorrower(msg.sender)) {
      revert NotApprovedBorrower();
    }
    address hooksInstance = parameters.hooks.hooksAddress();
    address hooksTemplate = getHooksTemplateForInstance[hooksInstance];
    // @audit only check if the template is registered, not if it is disabled
    if (hooksTemplate == address(0)) {
      revert HooksInstanceNotFound();
    }
    HooksTemplate memory templateDetails = _templateDetails[hooksTemplate];
    market = _deployMarket(
      parameters,
      hooksData,
      hooksTemplate,
      templateDetails,
      salt,
      originationFeeAsset,
      originationFeeAmount
    );
  }
```

The [`deploymarket()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-wildcat/blob/main/src/HooksFactory.sol#L393) function does not do any checks on `templateDetails.enabled`. As a result any user can deploy a market on a disabled hooks instance.

Example scenario:

- User A knows that template X will be disabled.
- User A deploys several hooks preemptively.
- Admin disables the template by calling [`disableHooksTemplate()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-wildcat/blob/main/src/HooksFactory.sol#L201).
- User A can deploy new markets on the disabled template using the predeployed instances.

Alternatively a user can just keep deploying markets on his own hooks instance.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add this change:

```diff
  function deployMarket(
    DeployMarketInputs calldata parameters,
    bytes calldata hooksData,
    bytes32 salt,
    address originationFeeAsset,
    uint256 originationFeeAmount
  ) external override nonReentrant returns (address market) {
    if (!IWildcatArchController(_archController).isRegisteredBorrower(msg.sender)) {
      revert NotApprovedBorrower();
    }
    address hooksInstance = parameters.hooks.hooksAddress();
    address hooksTemplate = getHooksTemplateForInstance[hooksInstance];
    if (hooksTemplate == address(0)) {
      revert HooksInstanceNotFound();
    }

+   if (!template.enabled) {
+     revert HooksTemplateNotAvailable();
+   }

    HooksTemplate memory templateDetails = _templateDetails[hooksTemplate];
    market = _deployMarket(
      parameters,
      hooksData,
      hooksTemplate,
      templateDetails,
      salt,
      originationFeeAsset,
      originationFeeAmount
    );
  }
```


